---
import {} from '../color-math.ts';
import { sourceLinks } from '../color-reference.ts';
---

<div class="color-hub">
  <a class="color-hub-card" href="/color-math/converter">
    <div class="color-spectrum" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <h2>Color-space converter</h2>
    <p>
      sRGB, linear sRGB, HSL, HSV, CIE XYZ, CIELAB, and Oklab. See the same
      color in each coordinate system.
    </p>
    <span>Convert colors →</span>
  </a>
  <a class="color-hub-card" href="/color-math/image">
    <canvas
      id="color-hub-example"
      aria-label="Built-in still-life example with colored objects and neutral swatches"
    ></canvas>
    <h2>Image adjustments</h2>
    <p>
      Compare linear-light and encoded-sRGB operations on a built-in scene, a
      test chart, or your own image.
    </p>
    <span>Adjust an image →</span>
  </a>
</div>
<section class="color-reference">
  <h2>Encoded values and light</h2>
  <p>
    An sRGB channel value of 0.5 decodes to approximately 0.214 in linear light.
    Multiplying encoded values and multiplying light values therefore produce
    different results.
  </p>
  <p>
    The image tool makes this distinction explicit and shows the operation
    order. Conversion results retain values outside the sRGB gamut; display
    previews clip them.
  </p>
  <p>
    <Fragment set:html={sourceLinks} />
  </p>
</section>
